        "hint": "BMI",
        "read_only": true,
        "label_info_title": "About BMI",
        "label_info_text": "What it is: Body Mass Index — a quick way to check whether a client's weight is healthy for their height.\n\nThe machine fills this in for you when you enter weight (kg) and height (cm).\n\nWhat the numbers mean:\nUnderweight: less than 18.5 — talk to the client about eating enough balanced food.\nNormal: 18.5 to 24.9 — encourage them to keep up healthy habits.\nOverweight: 25 to 29.9 — talk about more activity, less sugar and salt, and smaller portions.\nObese: 30 or more — flag the client to follow up at the facility.\n\nBMI is a guide, not a diagnosis. A very muscular person can have a high BMI without being unhealthy. Always look at the whole client.",
